## 12. Executed checks (candidate, isolated) — summary [EXECUTED]

Full code, receipts, stdout digests, and scope limits in `witnesses.json`. All use tiny synthetic data only; **none proves large-dataset or full-runtime behavior**.

- **W1 preview-vs-full inference trap** (exec `exec-lhb85rd5`, exit 0): 20-row preview inferred INTEGER; full scan found 2 TEXT + 1 NULL; conflicting rows quarantined with line numbers; kept+quarantined == total.
- **W2 deterministic vs stable ordering & identity** (exec `exec-15rdc9md`, exit 0): key-only stable sort is input-order dependent (sequence digests differ across permutations); content tie-break is permutation-invariant; identity scheme = sequence digest + order-insensitive multiset digest.
- **W3 freshness state machine** (first attempt exec `exec-x8rt9so3` **exit 1** — my check code resolved refs by variable name against cell ids, and one expectation was wrong; corrected rerun exec `exec-9l7v0rcz`, exit 0): clean run all `current`; edit-upstream → edited cell + dependents `stale`; kernel restart → old outputs `unverified` (never `current`); interrupted replay → cell `failed`, dependents `unverified`. Both attempts are recorded.
- **W4 streaming malformed handling + atomic save** (exec `exec-iv76_h6q`, exit 0): 500 synthetic NDJSON records in 5 chunks; 3 malformed/missing-field lines quarantined with line numbers (none dropped); O(1)-state streaming mean matches the in-memory reference; interrupted save left the previous committed manifest readable, tmp file ignored until the commit marker moved.

